Title: SPHEREx confirms predictions for artificial satellite trail pollution in Low Earth Orbit
Authors: Alejandro S. Borlaff - NASA Ames Research Center
Table: Properties of the population of observed satellite trails in SPHEREx observations
================================================================================
Byte-by-byte Description of file: table.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Bytes Format Units  Label     Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1-  4  I4     ---    Unnamed: 0      Description of Unnamed: 0
  6- 25  F20.16 deg    ra              [0.06/359.89] Average right ascension of the identified trail (degrees)
 27- 46  F20.16 deg    dec             [-87.57/88.64] Average declination of the identified trail (degrees)
 48- 68  F21.16 deg    pa              [-179.83/359.99] Position angle of the trail in equatorial coordinates (degrees, PA = 0 is North, + counter-clockwise).
 70- 86  A17    ---    OBSID           SPHEREx Observation ID
 88- 98  F11.5  ---    MJDOBS          [60796.0/60933.99] Modified Julian Date of the observation.
100-107  F8.4   s      XPOSURE         [113.58/113.59] Exposure (integration) time                
109-118  F10.6  deg    SGT_LAT_MIDPT   Ground track latitude at midpoint    
120-129  F10.6  deg    SGT_LON_MIDPT   Ground track longitude at midpoint   
131-140  F10.6  deg    SGT_MIN_GCD2SAA [0.43/133.91] Closest ground track dist to SAA   
142-151  F10.6  deg    SPS_ELON        Ecliptic longitude of planned telescope boresight 
153-162  F10.6  deg    SPS_ELAT        Ecliptic latitude of planned telescope boresight  
164-173  F10.6  deg    SPS_EPA         PA of FP y axis at planned boresight, E of ecl N  
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Notes: This table contains the properties (ID, location, position angle) of the identified artificial satellite trails in real SPHEREx images, obtained between May 2025 and September 2025.
